{
  // Type-check the VFS image builders. There was no config covering `images/`
  // at all, so every recipe under it was unchecked: a broken import or a
  // signature drift surfaced only when a builder was RUN, which needs a full
  // sysroot and a kernel and takes hours.
  //
  // Built before the change it is meant to check, deliberately. Lane V's own
  // hazard list says a gate written afterwards gets shaped to pass, and lane Y
  // is about to repoint thirteen of these files onto a new interface.
  //
  // ZERO ERRORS UNDER `images/` as of 2026-09-13. All four its first run found
  // are fixed:
  //
  //   * a StatResult passed where `{ ino, generation? }` was expected — fixed
  //     as a side effect of moving build-source-rootfs-shell-image.ts onto the
  //     Rust filesystem, whose 64-bit inode numbers the identity comparison
  //     now takes instead of silently comparing a bigint to a number;
  //   * `keyof typeof STAGING_FLAGS`, which is a Map's METHOD names and not
  //     its keys — the cast also asserted the flag is a KNOWN one, which is
  //     precisely what the next line checks, so removing it removed a lie;
  //   * `kind` left `unknown` by a ternary chain that narrows it for a reader
  //     but not for the compiler — now checked before use, which also retires
  //     an empty key list that stood in for "unsupported";
  //   * one introduced by this lane and fixed when it was introduced.
  //
  // STILL NOT WIRED AS A BLOCKING GATE, and the reason is no longer a
  // baseline. `tsc` exits non-zero on five errors in
  // `host/test/centralized-test-helper.ts`, which enters this program because
  // `images/vfs/scripts/generate-coreutils-man.ts` imports `runCentralizedProgram`
  // from it — a production build script depending on TEST scaffolding. Wiring
  // this means untangling that first, which is a real change to a script this
  // lane has not otherwise touched.
  //
  // It is useful as it stands: run it and require that the errors under
  // `images/` are exactly ZERO. Line numbers are deliberately not quoted — they
  // moved once already and a stale number reads as a different defect.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "module": "ESNext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "strict": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "ignoreDeprecations": "6.0",
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "lib": ["ES2024", "ES2024.SharedMemory", "DOM"],
    // Resolved from host/, which is where this repository installs its
    // TypeScript toolchain; there is no node_modules under images/.
    "typeRoots": ["../host/node_modules/@types"],
    "types": ["node"]
  },
  "include": ["vfs/**/*.ts", "rootfs/**/*.ts"]
}
